# Line endings
#
# The repository stores LF, and every working tree gets LF, regardless of a
# contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows checkout gets
# CRLF (core.autocrlf=true is the Git for Windows default), which contradicts
# .editorconfig's `end_of_line = lf` and made Prettier fail with a "Delete ␍"
# error on essentially every line of the project — 299 of 380 lint errors.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files Git must never run through line-ending conversion.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.zip   binary

# Compiled gettext catalogues, if translations are ever shipped.
*.mo    binary
